answers.body:
One possible solution to run each iteration of 2 different loops in parallel is using tasks. I suggest the following structure: #pragma omp parallel
#pragma omp single
{
    for(...) //first for loop
    {
        #pragma omp task
        {
            //loop body to run parallel
        }
    }

    for(...) //second for loop
    {
        #pragma omp task
        {
            //loop body to run parallel
        }
    }
} Note that The OpenMP runtime/compiler may decide not to defer the task, but run it immediately by the encountering thread. (The workload in your example is very small, so this may happen.) You have to make sure that the loop body is thread-safe and that the sharing attributes of all your variables are correctly set up. (e.g. cout is not thread-safe in your example)

