answers.body:
The problem is in your release implementation: if (!succ) {
      // if this compare-exchange fails, it loads the new value of tail
      // and stores it in p
      if (tail.compare_exchange_strong(p, nullptr, std::memory_order_acq_rel))
        return;

      do {
        succ = p->next.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
      } while (succ == nullptr);
    } As indicated by the comment, a failing compare-exchange overwrites the value in p . That of course is the reason why the following loop does not terminate as expected. The fix is quite simple: if (!succ) {
      auto expected = p;
      if (tail.compare_exchange_strong(expected, nullptr, std::memory_order_acq_rel))
        return;

      do {
        succ = p->next.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
      } while (succ == nullptr);
    }

