answers.body:
int myroutine(double *a, double *sum, int n)
{
    int i;
    static double localSum = *sum;

#pragma omp for reduction(+:localSum)
    for(i=0;i<n;i++){
        localSum += a[i];
    }
    *sum = localSum;

    return 0;
} works, but is gross and horrible, since it would break if you tried it from separate teams in a nested parallel region. (Though its safe if you're not using nested parallelism, and not starting OpenMP from independent pthreads, which is almost the same thing!) I would hope that something like #pragma omp for reduction(+:sum[0]) would work in OpenMP 5.0 where array sections are supported in reductions, but unfortunately compilers probably aren't there yet (understandably, since the specification  is not yet finalized!)

